# The tab bar
The Avatar page's tab bar:  Examples, Usage and API, each a notebook of this project.
Each notebook draws it under its title, `<avatar-tab-bar showing="usage"/>`, its own tab selected;  a click opens
another.  A view of several words is drawn by its element's name.

<spell-view "tab bar">
	<property "showing" one-of="examples, usage or api" description="Which notebook it's drawn in:  its tab is selected"/>

	<draw description="The tab strip a component page's tabs draw:  a segmented bar the width of the page, its tabs one size">
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="AvatarTabs" appearance="segmented" align="fluid" equal aria-label="Avatar">
				<ui-item link="/edit/@spell/notebooks/Avatar/Examples.spellx" selected={its showing is examples}>Examples</ui-item>
				<ui-item link="/edit/@spell/notebooks/Avatar/Usage.spellx" selected={its showing is usage}>Usage</ui-item>
				<ui-item link="/edit/@spell/notebooks/Avatar/API.spellx" selected={its showing is api}>API</ui-item>
			</ui-menu>
		</html>
	</draw>
</spell-view>
